WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.302
-My first guest
is a 17-time WWE champion

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:06.339
and one of the biggest
movie stars in the world.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.609
Now his life is the subject
of a new NBC comedy series

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.511
called "Young Rock,"

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:15.047
which premieres
February 16th at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.383
Here's the one and only
Dwayne Johnson.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.652
Ha ha!
It's the stud right there.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.487
That's what I'm talking about.
-My man.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.123
-That is what I'm talking about.
-Good to see you, brother.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.192
-It is great to see you, man.
You look great.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.628
You dedicate 100%
to every single thing you do,

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:31.564
and that's what
I love about you,

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.900
but you've always done that
since I've known you.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.169
Your new tequila, Teremana.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.405
By the way,
it is unbelievably delicious.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.507
That is a fantastic tequila.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:42.909
-It is unbelievable.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.311
I remember when
you first launched it,

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.146
I go,
"Dude, let's try this stuff."

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.615
It's my favorite.
It's unbelievable.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:53.019
-Yeah. I sent you some.
-Dude, it's empty. It's done.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.654
It's an empty box. It's great.

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:58.825
But you broke records
in its first year of business.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.960
-It was -- It was --
It was incredible.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.063
We wound up becoming --
We wound up breaking --

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:06.099
We wound up being the first --

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.735
the biggest launch
in the history of all spirits,

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.603
and that's all spirits
across the board.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:15.842
That's vodka, that's whiskey,
it's rum, it's -- it's gin.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.744
It was absolutely incredible.
-Yes!

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.912
-And to give you
a little bit of context,

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.582
we wound up selling
in less than a year

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.718
over 300,000 nine-liter cases.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.520
And when George Clooney
sold his tequila line,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.723
they were selling about 160,000.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.126
And we sold 300,000
in less than a year.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:35.061
I mean, it's just --
it's really crazy.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.129
But I got to tell you
something, you know.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:40.133
As you said, you do everything
like you do anything,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.168
and that's with 100% commitment.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.870
I wanted to make
good-quality tequila

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.605
for people
and bring people together.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.573
I wanted to make the tequila
for the people.

00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:48.875
-Good for you. I love it.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:52.144
I want to talk about
the show about your life.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:53.512
Let's talk about "Young Rock."

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:57.416
It premieres next Tuesday
here on NBC.

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:59.686
Was it you who realized
that your life could be a show?

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.121
Or did someone else
bring the idea to you

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.556
and you go, "Eh, could be"?

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:07.093
-You -- You know, there's guys
who I work very closely with

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:11.264
who you've met in the past,
as we're all buddies.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.766
And it --

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.002
I would travel with these guys
all across the country.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.403
And everywhere we would go --

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.339
and this is back
when I was wrestling.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.374
And I would wrestle
in a different town every night.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.109
We would all travel together.

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.910
And every time we would land,

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.646
every major city
across the country

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.248
I would say, "Yeah, you know,
see that gas station over there?

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.950
Well, you know,
that's where I bought

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.318
my first car from a crackhead."

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.519
"What?" "Yep."

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:36.222
And then the next town
we would go to, like,

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.857
"Yeah, you see that Motel 6?

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.859
Well, here's what
happened there."

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:42.795
So all these stories --
Finally, you know --

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.331
we started thinking,
"Well, I wonder...

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.667
creating a show
that has the lens of comedy

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.370
but to be able to share
the life lessons I've learned."

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.406
-You have three different actors
playing you

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.575
at the age of 10, 15, and 18.

00:02:56.575 --> 00:03:00.379
You also appear as yourself
in the year 2032

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:01.547
running for president.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:05.151
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.686
Don't ever change, dude.

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.387
Please promise me.
Just don't ever change.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.088
It is so fun.

00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:13.626
It is so fun to watch everything
you do, man. I love it.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:18.764
How did you decide that you
would tell the story that way?

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.400
-You know, it was --

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.668
Our show creator,
Nahnatchka Khan,

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.938
who's just such
a brilliant woman.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.939
We were trying
to figure out a way --

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:29.174
Well, first of all,
we wanted to figure out

00:03:29.174 --> 00:03:33.579
three points of my life
that were defining times.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:36.449
When I was 10 years old,
living here in Hawaii...

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.818
when I was 15 years old,
after multiple arrests

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:42.021
and doing a lot of things
I shouldn't have been doing...

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.456
and then when
I was 18 years old,

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.657
when I started to get my life
a little bit back on track,

00:03:45.657 --> 00:03:48.227
going to
the University of Miami.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.263
Then she had said,

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:54.900
"Well, ultimately the audience
is going to want to see you.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.704
What's the creative way that we
can infuse you into the show?"

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:00.006
So we sat for a few weeks.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.707
And it was her.
She came up with the idea.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:04.310
She said, "Well,
what if we set it in 2032

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.512
and you're running
for president?"

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.981
And I said, "I don't know.
It feels a little political."

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:11.350
She goes, "Well, there might be
a few people who might want

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.653
to see you run for president,
so think about it."

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.354
So I went home.
I talked to Lauren.

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:17.824
As you and I do, we go home,
we talk to our wives.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.424
-That's it.

00:04:19.424 --> 00:04:21.527
-Lauren said,
"I think you should do it.
I think it's great."

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.396
-That's the final stamp
you need.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.597
Also, the actors
who portray your parents

00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:26.999
on the show are great.

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:29.135
And you know I love your mom,
and I was gonna ask you --

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.870
-She loves you, by the way.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.173
-Did your mom weigh in on
casting for who should play her?

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.475
-She wanted to know --
I told her.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:38.978
I said, "Listen.
You're in good hands.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.647
I'm gonna cast someone
who I think you're really

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.216
gonna be really happy with."

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:46.452
And I said, "Mom, but just keep
in mind, we have to -- let's --

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.787
We have to be authentic
with our casting.

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:51.056
I want to make sure
that there's a woman

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:54.427
who is of Polynesian descent,
maybe Samoan descent."

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:58.397
She said, "Absolutely. I know
exactly who you should cast."

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.966
I said, "Who?"
She goes, "J.Lo."

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:02.401
Well...hold on.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:04.069
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:07.206
-Dude, my mom did the same --
I did a movie

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:11.176
where, in a flashback, my mom
was Sharon Stone in a movie.

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:14.379
And my mom told everyone that --
She's like,

00:05:14.379 --> 00:05:16.949
"Finally, someone did it right!

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.018
They cast Sharon Stone..."

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:20.652
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.652 --> 00:05:22.522
It's like -- Unbelievable.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:26.825
It was so -- It's just the best.

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:29.328
I just saw a video.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.497
You know, I love
watching your Instagrams.

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:35.068
And there was a video that
you posted that was beautiful.

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:37.703
And it was you and your mom

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:42.141
sitting at the headstone
of your grandparents in Hawaii

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.243
and singing this beautiful song.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.478
But your mom played
great ukulele.

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:48.414
And I go, "Wait. What?!"

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.817
I did not know
that she could play --

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:52.885
Your mom plays the ukulele?

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:57.289
-Oh, yes. She is -- She --

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:58.958
Hey.

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.694
Get my mom really quickly and
tell her to bring the ukulele.

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.662
It's right there
on the inside of the door.

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:06.332
-What? Does she --
-Mom!

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:09.668
No. Get the ukulele.
-Okay. Got it.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.169
-Is your mom there?

00:06:11.169 --> 00:06:13.205
-She's right here.
Here. Come here.

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:15.374
Okay. Good. Put that down.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.175
-Yeah.
-Okay. Come here. Come here.

00:06:17.175 --> 00:06:19.378
I want you to say hello
to somebody you know.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.781
-Who? Ohh!
-It's Jimmy Fallon.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:25.351
-Hi! Oh, my gosh!
Mom, you're gorgeous!

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.487
So good -- Good to see you.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:29.088
-Do you remember me?
-Are you kidd--

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.856
From our bit. New Year's.
Happy New Year.

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.425
I remember our bit.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:35.695
-I know. I know.
Do you remember what you did?

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:38.064
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:40.366
-Dude, I remember laying --

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:43.636
I remember laying on the ground
pretending I was passed out.

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:45.571
-I know.
-We were holding empty --

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.772
-That was awesome.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:49.008
-We were holding empty bottles
of champagne.

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:51.076
Oh, you were so funny.
-We had the best time.

00:06:51.076 --> 00:06:52.678
-That was the best.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:55.114
-Lauren's mom and I, we had
the best time that night.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:57.984
-Dude. And she constantly --
-We didn't expect you.

00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:00.485
We didn't know you were going
to be there with your wife.

00:07:00.485 --> 00:07:02.855
-She called me. "Jimmy's here,
and we're doing this!"

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:05.057
I was like, "Okay, Ma.
Tell him I said hello.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:08.227
But come on. Don't bother him.
Don't bother Jimmy."

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.062
-We had so much fun.
-I said, "Okay, I won't."

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.064
-No, no.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.600
Honestly, seriously, Dwayne,
your mom was fantastic.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.335
She was so --
-We had a good time.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:18.337
-We had the best time.
But I just want --

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.639
I was just talking about you
playing the ukulele.

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:22.641
Did not know that
you played the ukulele.

00:07:22.641 --> 00:07:24.376
Obviously,
how would I guess this?

00:07:24.376 --> 00:07:27.245
-He was asking -- When we went
to visit Grandma and Grandpa --

00:07:27.245 --> 00:07:29.948
-Oh, did you see that?
-It was the most beautiful --

00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:33.352
-I told him that --
-Every time we come to Hawaii,

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.488
we go up to visit
my parents, yeah.

00:07:35.488 --> 00:07:38.056
-It was beautiful.
-She has -- Let's --

00:07:38.056 --> 00:07:40.359
-I have mu ukulele.
-I know.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.562
-Let's sing him a song
real quick. Go ahead.

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:45.264
-Okay, okay, okay. I got a song.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:48.800
♪♪

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.769
-Oh. Sure. Okay.
-Okay.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:54.172
♪♪

00:07:54.172 --> 00:07:57.743
♪ Savalivali means
go for a walk ♪

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:01.380
♪ Tautalatala means
too much talk ♪

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:04.983
♪ Alofa ia te oe
means I love you ♪

00:08:04.983 --> 00:08:08.087
♪ Take it easy, faifai lemu ♪

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.655
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.823
-Oh, my goodness! Come on!
Are you joking me?!

00:08:11.823 --> 00:08:14.059
-We have one more.
-No, we don't have one more!

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:15.794
what do you mean,
we have one more?

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:18.697
What is this? What's happening?

00:08:18.697 --> 00:08:21.300
♪♪

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.538
-♪ We love you, Jimmy,
oh, yes, we do ♪

00:08:25.538 --> 00:08:27.739
-Okay. I'll go with it.

00:08:27.739 --> 00:08:33.145
♪ We love you, Jimmy,
and that is true ♪

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:36.748
♪ When we're away from you ♪

00:08:36.748 --> 00:08:39.384
♪ We're blue ♪

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:44.890
♪ Oh, Jimmy, we love you ♪

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.259
-Oh, my! I love you!
-Good job, Mom. Good job.

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:49.228
-I'm sending love
right back to you.

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:51.396
Mom just crushed, by the way!

00:08:51.396 --> 00:08:54.466
You just stole the interview.
You're unbelievable.

00:08:54.466 --> 00:08:56.568
You are a superstar.
-I love when she goes --

00:08:56.568 --> 00:08:58.471
I love when she goes,
"We got one more!"

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:02.041
I'm like, "What? We do?"
"We love you, Jimmy!"

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:04.110
-That was unbelievable.
-Good to see you, Jimmy.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.278
-You're gorgeous.
It's great to see you.

00:09:06.278 --> 00:09:09.081
And, yeah, happy new year again.
Let's do it again.

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:10.682
Guys, come on back.

00:09:10.682 --> 00:09:12.418
We have more "Tonight Show"
when we come back.

00:09:12.418 --> 00:09:13.586
Come on. We're going to talk
"Young Rock."

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:15.988
-Say hi to your lovely wife.
-I will.

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:17.623
-Leave, Ma!
-Okay.

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:19.692
-[ Laughter ]
-Mwah!

